{"uid":"synthetic_dataset.py","name":"synthetic_dataset.py","qualname":"synthetic_dataset.py","kind":"module","file":"synthetic_dataset.py","line":1,"end_line":707,"language":"py","signature":"","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Synthetic Dataset Generator for TopoGPT2.","description":"Generates high-quality code instruction-tuning data from existing source files\nusing a multi-stage LLM pipeline:\n\n    file → analysis → spec → chain-of-thought → vague question → JSONL\n\nEach sample (JSONL line) contains:\n{\n    \"instruction\":  \"vague natural question\",\n    \"thinking\":     \"chain-of-thought reasoning\",\n    \"spec\":         \"detailed spec-driven prompt\",\n    \"todo\":         [\"task 1\", \"task 2\", ...],\n    \"response\":     \"```language\noriginal clean code\n```\",\n    \"file_path\":    \"src/foo/bar.py\",\n    \"lang\":         \"python\",\n    \"checksum\":     \"sha256 of original code\",\n}\n\nPipeline is designed for efficiency:\n- One LLM call per file (master prompt, one-shot)\n- Streaming JSONL writes (never holds full dataset in memory)\n- SHA256 dedup across the full corpus\n- Resumable: tracks processed files in a manifest\n- Batch-friendly: process N files per run\n\nBackend: Groq API (Llama-3.3-70B, fastest/cheapest) or OpenRouter.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"","members":["synthetic_dataset.py::LLMBackend","synthetic_dataset.py::GroqBackend","synthetic_dataset.py::OpenRouterBackend","synthetic_dataset.py::OllamaBackend","synthetic_dataset.py::build_backend","synthetic_dataset.py::validate_sample","synthetic_dataset.py::ProcessedManifest","synthetic_dataset.py::SyntheticDatasetGenerator","synthetic_dataset.py::build_logger","synthetic_dataset.py::parse_args","synthetic_dataset.py::load_paths","synthetic_dataset.py::main"],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
